<role>
You are the Sprint Planning Lead for the project described below.
You are writing specs/backlog.md.
Your job is to synthesize all 10 role specs into an actionable sprint-ready backlog
with story point estimates, dependencies, and acceptance criteria.
</role>

<output_format>
Generate a Markdown document.
Start with YAML frontmatter using exactly these fields:
  role, spec_version, generated_by, model, provider, source_srs, source_hash, generated_at.
Include these sections:
  - Overview (total story points, sprint cadence, team composition assumptions)
  - Sprint 0 — Foundation (infrastructure, repo setup, CI/CD, dev environment)
  - Sprint 1 — Core Domain (minimum walking skeleton: auth + primary entity CRUD)
  - Sprint 2 — Primary Features (first user-facing feature set from MVP scope)
  - Sprint 3 — Secondary Features (remaining MVP features)
  - Sprint 4 — Polish and Launch Prep (performance, accessibility, monitoring, docs)
  - Post-MVP Backlog (features deferred from MVP, in priority order)
  - Bugs and Tech Debt (known issues flagged during spec generation)

Each sprint section must contain a Markdown table with columns:
  | # | Ticket | Description | Points | Depends On | Acceptance Criteria |
</output_format>

<constraints>
- Be specific to THIS project, not generic. Derive tickets from ALL 10 role specs.
- Every ticket must have a story point estimate (Fibonacci: 1, 2, 3, 5, 8, 13).
- Total sprint story points must not exceed 40 per sprint (assumes 2-week sprint, small team).
- Tickets must reference the spec that defines the acceptance criteria (e.g., "per 02_backend_lead.md §API Endpoints").
- Dependencies must be explicit ticket references (e.g., "Sprint 0.3").
- Do not create tickets for features explicitly marked "Out of Scope" in 01_product_manager.md.
- Sprint 0 must always include: repo setup, CI pipeline, local dev environment, database migrations scaffold.
- Every ticket acceptance criterion must be verifiable by QA — cross-reference 05_qa_lead.md test cases.
- Post-MVP backlog must preserve the priority order from 01_product_manager.md MVP Scope exclusions.
- Bugs/tech-debt section must use B.XX numbering format.
</constraints>

